## 7. Cross-cutting concerns: Production Readiness Review

### A. Feature enablement and rollback
- _How can this feature be enabled/disabled at runtime?_
- _Does enabling/disabling require a restart? A redeploy?_
- _Tests for enablement/disablement?_
- _If enabled then disabled, is the system back to a clean state?_

### B. Rollout, upgrade, and rollback planning
- _How can rollout fail? Can it impact already-running workloads?_
- _What signals trigger a rollback?_
- _Is the rollback plan tested in dev/staging?_
- _Release-time migrations needed?_

### C. Monitoring requirements
- _Metrics emitted for success/failure?_
- _Logs emitted? PII scrubbed?_
- _Alerts configured?_
- _Dashboards visualizing health?_

### D. Dependencies
- _External services / APIs? Failure behavior when each is down?_
- _Contractual SLAs we depend on?_

### E. Scalability
- _Fastest-growing scaling vector?_
- _Projected load at MVP launch / 6 months / year 1?_
- _Bottlenecks (DB connections, LLM rate limits, memory, CPU)?_
- _Plan when we hit 80% of any quota?_

### F. Troubleshooting
- _On-call diagnosis at 3am?_
- _Most likely failure mode, what it looks like in dashboards?_
- _Runbook location? Maintainer?_

### G. Security and compliance
- _New attack surface?_
- _Auth model for new endpoints?_
- _Privileged operations and who can perform them?_
- _Audit events logged?_

_Each item: filled in OR explicit N/A with reason. Silent absence forbidden._

